# Story 102: Multi-Workspace in Desktop (40s)
# Hook: Many workspaces, one window. The desktop app stacks them two rows high.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-102-multi-workspace-desktop.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 5

[00:00.0 --> 00:05.0]
Many workspaces, one window. The desktop app stacks them two rows high.

[00:05.0 --> 00:14.0]
The desktop header has two rows. The top row lists your workspaces; the row below lists the tabs inside the workspace you have selected.

[00:14.0 --> 00:23.0]
Click a workspace up top to switch your entire context -- a different project, a different upstream, a different set of tabs and panes.

[00:23.0 --> 00:32.0]
The desktop app also surfaces voice prompting and a dedicated pipeline output panel, so multi-stage runs are visible right beside your panes.

[00:32.0 --> 00:40.0]
One window, every workspace -- the desktop app is built for juggling projects.

